.TH OPENROUTER-CREDITS-TRAY 1 "" "openrouter-credits-tray" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
openrouter-credits-tray \- show the remaining OpenRouter credit in the system tray
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B openrouter-credits-tray
.RB [ \-\-delay
.IR seconds ]
.br
.B openrouter-credits-tray
.RB \-\-settings " | " \-\-check " | " \-\-clear\-key " | " \-\-version
.br
.B openrouter-credits-tray
.B \-\-set\-key
.RI [ key ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B openrouter-credits-tray
shows the remaining credit of an OpenRouter account as a badge in the system
tray, using the StatusNotifierItem (Ayatana AppIndicator) protocol. The badge is
green above $2, amber above $0.50 and red below that. Clicking it opens a menu
with usage details, a manual refresh, the Settings form and an option to start
on login.
.PP
Only one tray runs per user. Starting it again while it is running opens the
Settings form instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-delay " seconds"
Wait before creating the tray icon. Used by the login autostart entry.
.TP
.B \-\-settings
Open the Settings form, where the API key and refresh interval are set, and exit
when it is closed.
.TP
.BR \-\-set\-key " [\fIkey\fR]"
Store the API key in the desktop keyring and exit. Without an argument the key
is read from a hidden prompt, so it does not appear in the process list or the
shell history.
.TP
.B \-\-clear\-key
Remove the stored API key from the keyring and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Print where the API key was found and the current balance, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short help text and exit.
.SH API KEY
The key is looked up in this order: the desktop keyring (Secret Service), the
.B OPENROUTER_API_KEY
environment variable, then the config file. A key found in the config file is
moved into the keyring on the next start.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OPENROUTER_API_KEY
API key, used when the keyring holds none.
.TP
.B OPENROUTER_TRAY_INTERVAL
Refresh interval in seconds (default 300, minimum 30). A value in the config
file takes precedence.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/openrouter-credits/config
Settings that are not secret, such as the refresh interval.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/openrouter-credits-tray.desktop
Per-user start on login entry, or an override that disables the system one.
.TP
.I /etc/xdg/autostart/openrouter-credits-tray.desktop
System-wide start on login entry.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/icons/hicolor/*/apps/openrouter-credits-*.png
Generated badge icons.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/Fax/openrouter-credits-tray
